Fixes #656 

## Changes

- A new set of base design tokens for typography: font-sizes
- These base design tokens are then used in the base responsive typography
- Also used to create utility classes that apply a specific font-size from the base design tokens, at a specific breakpoint
- Adds utility classes that output responsive font-sizes at each specified breakpoint
- Updating docs to match updated typography
- Adds `responsive-font-size.get()` mixin

### Details

There’s now a single list of base design tokens for font-sizes:

```scss
$font-sizes: (
  '1': 0.8rem,
  '2': 1rem,
  '3': 1.25rem,
  '4': 1.45rem,
  '5': 1.7rem,
  '6': 2rem,
  '7': 3rem,
  '8': 4.8rem,
)
```

Those are used to create responsive typography for the elements `h1` – `h6`, and for classes `.u-h1` – `.u-h6` (in the same way as before):

```scss
$font-sizes: (
  '#{setup.$no-media-query}': (
    'h1': font-size.get('6'),
    'h2': font-size.get('5'),
    'h3': font-size.get('4'),
    'h4': font-size.get('3'),
    'h5': font-size.get('2'),
    'h6': font-size.get('1'),
    'body': font-size.get('2'),
  ),
  'm': (
    'h1': font-size.get('8'),
    'h2': font-size.get('7'),
    'h3': font-size.get('6'),
    'h4': font-size.get('4'),
    'h5': font-size.get('2'),
    'h6': font-size.get('1'),
    'body': font-size.get('2'),
  ),
)
```

```css
h1 {
  font-size: 2rem;
}
h2 {
  font-size: 1.7rem;
}
h3 {
  font-size: 1.45rem;
}
@media screen and (min-width: 30em) {
  h1 {
    font-size: 4.8rem;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 3rem;
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 2rem;
  }
}
```

and:

```css
.u-h1 {
  font-size: 2rem;
}
.u-h2 {
  font-size: 1.7rem;
}
.u-h3 {
  font-size: 1.45rem;
}
@media screen and (min-width: 30em) {
  .u-h1 {
    font-size: 4.8rem;
  }
  .u-h2 {
    font-size: 3rem;
  }
  .u-h3 {
    font-size: 2rem;
  }
}
```

They’re also used to create utility classes that apply a single font-size at a specific breakpoint, to be used to create exceptions to the responsive typography:

```css
.u-text-6 {
  font-size: 2rem;
}
.u-text-7 {
  font-size: 3rem;
}
.u-text-8 {
  font-size: 4.8rem;
}
@media screen and (min-width: 30em) {
  .u-text-6@m {
    font-size: 2rem;
  }
  .u-text-7@m {
    font-size: 3rem;
  }
  .u-text-8@m {
    font-size: 4.8rem;
  }
}
```

There’s a Sass function to return a specific font-size from the base font-sizes. There’s a new Sass mixin that outputs the responsive font-sizes — a font-size declaration wrapped in a media-query for each that’s declared for e.g. h3

```scss
@use '~bitstyles/scss/bitstyles/tools/responsive-font-size';

.component-class::after {
  @include responsive-font-size.get('h4');
}
```

gives:

```css
.component-class::after {
  font-size: 1.25rem;
}

@media screen and (min-width: 30em) {
  .component-class::after {
    font-size: 1.45rem;
  }
}
```

